/*
:name: port_type_not_a_type
:type: error
:error: `Nope_t` is not a type
:help: declare it with `type Nope_t
*/

// Suggestions 2.3 row 6b: a PORT type that names no declared type must be the
// same compile error a typed local already gets (`mut a:Nope_t = b` ->
// "`Nope_t` is not a type (no such `type`/`enum` is declared or in scope)").
// Today the port slot is never checked: `top` compiles with exit 0 and cgen
// emits `input signed a` -- a ONE-bit signed port -- which is also how every
// unresolved imported alias (imported_alias_port_width) silently shrank.
pub mod top(a:Nope_t, b:U8) -> (y:U8@[]) {  // locate_error_here
  y = a ^ b
}
